          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "failed-protected-token-check",
          "text": "## GEIPAN Testimonies: November 11, 1980\n\nMultiple reports of **unidentified flying objects (UFOs)** were recorded across France on November 11, 1980. Below is a list of locations and associated reports:\n\n**Chamonix (73) to Grenoble (38)**\n\n* **11/11/1980, T1-T3:**  Multiple witnesses reported seeing a bright, fast-moving object with a pulsating light.  (PV n°1133 (1980308411).pdf )\n\n**Corsica (2A, 2B)**\n\n* **11/11/1980, T1-T3:**  Similar reports of bright, fast-moving objects with pulsating lights. (PV n°1253 (1980308413).pdf )\n\n**Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur (04, 06, 13)**\n\n* **11/11/1980, T1-T12:**  Numerous reports of UFOs, often described as bright, disc-shaped objects with lights, moving at high speeds. Some witnesses reported multiple UFOs. (Multiple PV numbers, including167 (1980208579).pdf,177 (1980309804).pdf,367 (1980308423).pdf,599 (1980308437).pdf, and752 (1980308420).pdf)\n\n**Rhône-Alpes (43, 38, 73)**\n\n* **11/11/1980, T1-T12:** Similar reports to other regions, with witnesses describing bright, fast-moving objects with lights. (Multiple PV numbers)\n\n**Other Regions**\n\n* **11/11/1980, T1-T3:** Reports of UFOs seen in:\n    *  Aullene (2A)\n    *  Muret (38)\n    *  Castres (81)\n    *  Theoule-sur-Mer (06)\n    *  Marignane (13)\n    *  Arcs (83)\n    *  Seyssinet-Pariset (38)\n    *  Esplantas (43)\n    *  Puy-en-Velay (43)\n    *  Saint-Jean-de-Maurienne (73)\n    *  Bonnieux (84)\n    *  Pianottoli-Caldarello (20)",
          "translation_text_sha256": "f2124d5cb9e2e113803ac9fb0f3b9e28af913a5f91c3c10384639c276d62734c"
        },
